<title>SWEDEN: SSAB Q1 profit falls 44 pct.</title>
<headline>SSAB Q1 profit falls 44 pct.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-04-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish steel group SSAB presented these first quarter earnings for the period ending March 31.</p>
<p>				  (million crowns unless stated)</p>
<p> Profit after fin items		  470   vs   844</p>
<p> Turnover				  4,325   vs 4,701</p>
<p> Earnings per share (crowns)	  2.60   vs  4.70</p>
<p> Costs				     3,710   vs 3,786</p>
<p> Depreciation				194   vs   180</p>
<p> Associated interest			16   vs    16</p>
<p> Operating profit			  437   vs   751</p>
<p> Net financial items			33   vs    93</p>
<p> Tax					   129   vs   234</p>
<p> Minorities			CHARGE    8   vs    10  CHARGE</p>
<p>NOTE - A Reuter poll of 11 analysts had forecast a first quarter profit after financial items of 470 million crowns.</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700-1017</p>
</text>
